WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:08.292
People sitting near the courtroom doors began to sneeze.

2
00:00:08.293 --> 00:00:11.287
"I know who the next witness is!" Alice said.

3
00:00:11.288 --> 00:00:14.113
"It must be the Duchess' cook."

4
00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:15.976
Alice was correct.

5
00:00:15.977 --> 00:00:20.400
The Cook entered the courtroom, carrying her pepper shaker.

6
00:00:20.401 --> 00:00:25.130
"Tell us your story!" the King commanded.

7
00:00:25.131 --> 00:00:30.401
"No, I refuse!" The Cook crossed her arms.

8
00:00:30.402 --> 00:00:33.572
The King didn't know what to do.

9
00:00:33.573 --> 00:00:37.502
He looked at the White Rabbit for advice.

10
00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:44.048
"Your Majesty, you must get this witness to tell her story," the White Rabbit said.

11
00:00:44.049 --> 00:00:48.574
"The Knave of Hearts is accused of stealing the Queen's tarts.

12
00:00:48.575 --> 00:00:50.712
This woman is a cook.

13
00:00:50.713 --> 00:00:54.344
She knows all about tarts."

14
00:00:54.345 --> 00:01:00.779
"Well, if I must, then I must," the King said.

15
00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:04.588
Then he frowned at the Cook for a long time.

16
00:01:04.589 --> 00:01:10.177
Finally he said, "What are tarts made of?"

17
00:01:10.178 --> 00:01:15.120
"Mostly pepper," the Cook said.

18
00:01:15.121 --> 00:01:20.939
"Molasses," said a sleepy voice behind her.

19
00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:24.972
"Seize that Dormouse!" the Queen shrieked.

20
00:01:24.973 --> 00:01:27.951
"Remove that Dormouse from court!

21
00:01:27.952 --> 00:01:34.235
Off with his head! Off with his whiskers!"

22
00:01:34.236 --> 00:01:41.433
For a few minutes, the whole courtroom was in confusion as the Dormouse was removed.

23
00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:47.129
By the time everyone settled down again, the Cook had disappeared.

24
00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:50.281
"Forget about the Cook."

25
00:01:50.282 --> 00:01:55.246
The King sounded relieved that he didn't have to deal with her anymore.

26
00:01:55.247 --> 00:01:59.119
"Really, my dear," he whispered to the Queen.

27
00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:03.035
"You must question the next witness.

28
00:02:03.036 --> 00:02:08.226
Dealing with all these people is making my head hurt."

29
00:02:08.227 --> 00:02:12.968
"No, it's your job," the Queen said firmly.

30
00:02:12.969 --> 00:02:17.248
Alice watched the White Rabbit hold up his scroll of paper.

31
00:02:17.249 --> 00:02:21.940
"They really don't have any evidence against the Knave of Hearts yet," she thought.

32
00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:24.966
"I wonder who the next witness will be."

33
00:02:24.967 --> 00:02:28.628
"Alice!" the White Rabbit called loudly.

34
00:02:28.629 --> 00:02:33.307
Alice jumped when she heard her name on the White Rabbit's scroll.

35
00:02:33.308 --> 00:02:38.440
"Here!" Alice leaped to her feet, forgetting how large she'd grown.

36
00:02:38.441 --> 00:02:43.453
She knocked over the jury box, and all the jurors tumbled out.

37
00:02:43.454 --> 00:02:46.785
"Oh, I'm so sorry!" Alice cried.

38
00:02:46.786 --> 00:02:50.488
Last week she'd knocked over a bowl of goldfish.

39
00:02:50.489 --> 00:02:53.488
This accident reminded her of that.

40
00:02:53.489 --> 00:03:00.256
She felt as if she had to put the jurors back quickly, or they'd die.

41
00:03:00.257 --> 00:03:03.148
The King scowled at Alice.

42
00:03:03.149 --> 00:03:13.269
"This trial cannot go on until the jurors are back in their proper places."

43
00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:16.803
Alice began working on it.

44
00:03:16.804 --> 00:03:21.373
But then she realized she'd put a lizard in upside down.

45
00:03:21.374 --> 00:03:24.155
She put the creature right side up.

46
00:03:24.156 --> 00:03:28.313
"Putting the jurors back is actually very silly," Alice thought.

47
00:03:28.314 --> 00:03:32.614
"None of these creatures will be much help at this trial."

48
00:03:32.615 --> 00:03:36.324
The jurors' slates were found and returned to them.

49
00:03:36.325 --> 00:03:39.451
They all began to write about the accident.

50
00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:43.752
All except the lizard, who stared at the ceiling.

51
00:03:43.753 --> 00:03:50.535
"What do you know about this tart business?" the King asked Alice.

52
00:03:50.536 --> 00:03:52.889
"Nothing," Alice replied.

53
00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:56.538
"Nothing at all?" the King asked.

54
00:03:56.539 --> 00:04:00.089
"Nothing at all," she repeated.

55
00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:05.570
For a few minutes, the jurors kept writing on their slates.

56
00:04:05.571 --> 00:04:08.513
The King wrote in a notebook.

57
00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:15.742
Suddenly he called out, "Silence!" even though no one was talking.

58
00:04:15.743 --> 00:04:18.415
He read aloud from his notebook.

59
00:04:18.416 --> 00:04:27.476
"'Rule 42: All people more than a mile high must leave the courtroom.'"

60
00:04:27.477 --> 00:04:33.751
Everyone stared at Alice. "I'm not a mile high."

61
00:04:33.752 --> 00:04:37.722
"Yes, you are," the King said.

62
00:04:37.723 --> 00:04:42.158
"Almost two miles high," the Queen added.

63
00:04:42.159 --> 00:04:45.088
"Well, I'm not leaving," Alice said.

64
00:04:45.089 --> 00:04:49.628
"Besides, that's not a real rule; you just made it up."

65
00:04:49.629 --> 00:04:54.980
"It's the oldest rule in the book," the King said.

66
00:04:54.981 --> 00:04:59.060
"Then it should be Rule One," Alice replied.

67
00:04:59.061 --> 00:05:04.533
The King shook with anger.

68
00:05:04.534 --> 00:05:09.874
"Jury, what is your verdict?"

